PulseAudio RAOP discovery: load each speaker's sink with autoreconnect=1.

Without it a sink whose connection drops while it plays (the speaker closes RTSP, the stream
restarts) unloads itself, but module-raop-discover keeps the speaker in its table, so the
speaker's next announcement looks like one already loaded and the sink never comes back: the
HomePod vanished from the list on 2026-11-01. With it the sink reconnects instead.

--- a2/src/modules/raop/module-raop-discover.c
+++ b2/src/modules/raop/module-raop-discover.c
@@ -347,7 +347,9 @@
         latency = u->latency;
 
     t = args;
-    args = pa_sprintf_malloc("%s latency_msec=%u", args, latency);
+    /* autoreconnect: a sink whose connection drops unloads itself otherwise, while this module still
+     * counts the speaker as loaded, so it never comes back until avahi forgets and re-finds it */
+    args = pa_sprintf_malloc("%s latency_msec=%u autoreconnect=1", args, latency);
     pa_xfree(t);
 
     pa_log_debug("Loading module-raop-sink with arguments '%s'", args);
